// One subject, as the installation's conversation summaries name it
// (CLEAN-270, spec 038 research R7).
//
// Version 1 of the summary wrote "short topic tags": free text, a new
// spelling per conversation, so two conversations about one thing did not
// meet in any count. From version 2 the model chooses among the topics that
// already exist, by `key`, and may propose one new topic when none fits.
// ChatSession.topicIds holds what it chose.
//
// A topic is created only by the summary batch, one at a time: the batch is
// sequential and reads the vocabulary again for each conversation, so the
// topic one conversation coined is offered to the next.
//
// At most 100 of them stand (not merged) at once: past that a proposal is
// dropped and its conversation has no topic (`TOPICS_STANDING_MAX`, with
// the reason for the number). And none is coined from a conversation with
// an agent only the Owner manages: the vocabulary is shown to every
// operator, and such a conversation is nobody else's to read
// (`ChatInsightService`).
//
// `labels` is what people read, one entry per language of the app console
// ({ "en": "…", "ru": "…" }), 1 to 3 words each, written when the topic is
// coined. A reader that finds no entry for its language shows `en`.
//
// `mergedIntoId` is set when an operator folds this topic into another
// (merge_chat_topics): two labels turned out to mean one subject. Readers
// follow it once, and a merged topic is never offered to the model again.
// A plain column, no relation: nothing deletes a topic, and merging re-points
// whatever was folded into the merged one, so one step always arrives.
//
// No conversation count here. How much a topic is used is read from the
// conversations that carry it; a counter would be a second truth
// (docs/statistics.md).
model ChatTopic {
  id           String   @id @default(uuid())
  // Lower-case English slug; what the model chooses between.
  key          String   @unique
  labels       Json
  mergedIntoId String?
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
}
